; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Rendered by Terraform (pgbouncer.tf) and mounted into the PgBouncer pod at
; /bitnami/pgbouncer/conf/userlist.txt, alongside pgbouncer.ini.tftpl.
;
; Plaintext-password entries ("user" "password") rather than pre-hashed
; SCRAM/MD5 secrets -- PgBouncer hashes them on the fly for both the
; client<->pgbouncer and pgbouncer<->postgres legs. The plaintext value lives
; only in Terraform state (gitignored, same posture as every other generated
; password in this repo) and in this rendered file inside a Kubernetes Secret,
; never in a tracked file.
;
; Two entries, and no application (ADR 0005): the Postgres superuser, which
; doubles as PgBouncer's admin_users entry for the `pgbouncer` pseudo-database
; admin console (SHOW POOLS etc., used by the readiness probe and by manual
; operator inspection), and the lookup role PgBouncer connects as to run
; auth_query. Every application role is authenticated from Postgres itself.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

"${admin_user}" "${admin_password}"
"${auth_user}" "${auth_password}"
